        "text": "Fig. 1 shows a torch that has been switched on, drawn inside a closed system, and the energy it gives out in one minute. The boxes are lettered **P**, **Q**, **R** and **S**.\n\n\n\n*Fig. 1: Energy flow in a torch that is switched on.*\n\n**(a)** Name the form of energy represented by EACH of the boxes **P**, **Q**, **R** and **S**.  **[4 marks]**\n\n**(b)** Use the values given in Fig. 1 to show that energy has been conserved in this closed system.  **[3 marks]**\n\n**(c)** (i) Which of **R** and **S** is the useful energy from a torch? Give a reason.  **[2 marks]**\n\n(ii) State what a pupil would notice about the torch after it has been left on for some time.  **[1 mark]**\n\n**(d)** Explain why the torch had to be drawn inside a **closed system** for this energy sum to work out exactly.  **[2 marks]**\n\n---"
