    "markingScheme": "*General rules: (1) Accept any other correct and relevant answer. (2) The names of the forms of energy must be correct and complete: chemical, electrical, heat (thermal), light, sound, kinetic, potential and nuclear. 'Power' or 'force' written for a form of energy earns no mark. (3) In an energy chain the forms must appear in the right order; one mark is lost for each form placed out of order. (4) In a calculation, award the working mark and the answer mark separately; the unit J must appear for the final mark. (5) Where a candidate gives more answers than are asked for, mark only the first ones up to the number required. (6) Do not deduct marks for spelling unless the meaning is changed.)*\n\n### Question 1 (12 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- P - **chemical energy** (1 mark).\n- Q - **electrical energy** (1 mark).\n- R - **light energy** (1 mark).\n- S - **heat (thermal) energy** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'Battery energy' or 'current' earns no mark.*\n\n**(b)** [3 marks]\n\n- **Energy supplied = 60 J** (1 mark).\n- **Energy given out = 15 J + 45 J = 60 J** (1 mark).\n- **The two totals are equal, so the energy has only been changed in form and none has been destroyed** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: The sum must be shown; a bare statement of the law earns the third mark only.*\n\n**(c)** [3 marks]\n\n- (i) **R, the light energy** (1 mark); **because the torch is used in order to give light** (1 mark).\n- (ii) **The torch feels warm (the cells or the bulb heat up)** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: Reason mark only if R is chosen.*\n\n**(d)** [2 marks]\n\n- **In a closed system no energy enters or leaves without being counted** (1 mark).\n- **So all the energy given out can be added up and shown to equal the energy supplied** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'It is covered' or 'it is in a box' alone earns no mark.*\n\n### Question 2 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- A - **solar (light) energy to electrical energy** (1 mark).\n- B - **electrical energy to heat energy** (1 mark).\n- C - **electrical energy to kinetic energy** (1 mark).\n- D - **chemical energy to electrical energy to sound energy** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: Accept 'electrical to sound' for D.*\n\n**(b)** [3 marks]\n\n- **Useful: kinetic energy of the blades** (1 mark).\n- **Wasted: sound energy and heat energy** (1 mark).\n- **The wasted energy spreads into the air and surroundings and cannot be used again** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'It is destroyed' earns no mark.*\n\n**(c)** [3 marks]\n\n- Any THREE of: **sunlight is free and renewable, so no fuel is bought**; **no smoke or carbon dioxide is given off**; **it makes no noise**; **it needs little maintenance** (1 mark each).\n  - *Marking note: 'It is modern' is not a scientific reason.*\n\n### Question 3 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [2 marks]\n\n- **Energy can neither be created nor destroyed** (1 mark).\n- **It can only be changed from one form to another (the total remains the same)** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: Both halves are needed for the full 2 marks.*\n\n**(b)** [3 marks]\n\n- **Potential energy of the stored water shown first** (1 mark).\n- **Kinetic energy of the falling water and of the turbine shown next** (1 mark).\n- **Electrical energy shown last, with the boxes joined by arrows in the correct order** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: A written chain with arrows is accepted in place of boxes.*\n\n**(c)** [3 marks]\n\n- (i) **1,000 J - 850 J** (1 mark) **= 150 J** (1 mark, unit required).\n- (ii) **Heat energy (accept sound energy)** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: A correct answer with no unit scores 1 of the 2 marks.*\n\n**(d)** [2 marks]\n\n- **The 150 J is not destroyed; it is changed into heat and sound** (1 mark).\n- **Counting every form, the total is still 1,000 J** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'The generator is weak' earns no mark.*\n\n### Question 4 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- Microphone - **sound to electrical** (1 mark).\n- Phone being charged - **electrical to chemical** (1 mark).\n- Candle burning - **chemical to heat and light** (1 mark).\n- Green plant - **l"
