        "text": "Fig. 1 shows four sources of plant nutrients brought to a school garden. They are lettered **W**, **X**, **Y** and **Z**. **W** is a heap of well-rotted plant remains, **X** is a sack of hard granules bought from an agro-chemical shop, **Y** is a basket of droppings from the school poultry house and **Z** is a bottle of fertilizer solution to be mixed with water.\n\n\n\n*Fig. 1: Four sources of plant nutrients brought to a school garden.*\n\n**(a)** State whether EACH of **W**, **X**, **Y** and **Z** is an organic or an inorganic source of plant nutrients.  **[4 marks]**\n\n**(b)** Describe TWO physical characteristics of **W** and TWO physical characteristics of **X**.  **[4 marks]**\n\n**(c)** Which of the four sources would have to be applied in the LARGEST quantity to supply a bed with enough nutrients? Give a reason for your answer.  **[2 marks]**\n\n---"
