    "markingScheme": "*General rules: (1) Accept any other correct and relevant answer. (2) The names of the components must be used correctly: cell or battery, switch, resistor, diode, LED, capacitor and inductor. 'Bulb' written for LED earns no mark. (3) In a circuit diagram, the recognised symbols must be used and the circuit must be complete; a broken circuit loses the completeness mark. (4) 'Thermal' is accepted for a station that burns fuel and 'nuclear' for one that splits atoms; the two must not be interchanged. (5) Where a candidate gives more answers than are asked for, mark only the first ones up to the number required. (6) Do not deduct marks for spelling unless the meaning is changed.)*\n\n### Question 1 (12 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- W - **battery (two dry cells in series)** (1 mark).\n- X - **switch** (1 mark).\n- Y - **resistor** (1 mark).\n- Z - **LED (light-emitting diode)** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'Bulb' or 'lamp' written for Z earns no mark.*\n\n**(b)** [4 marks]\n\n- W - **supplies the electrical energy (drives the current)** (1 mark).\n- X - **completes or breaks the circuit, switching the current on and off** (1 mark).\n- Y - **limits the current and so protects the LED** (1 mark).\n- Z - **gives out light when current passes through it** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'It carries current' is true of every part and earns no mark.*\n\n**(c)** [2 marks]\n\n- **No, the LED is not lit** (1 mark).\n- **The switch is open, so the circuit is incomplete and no current flows** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: No mark for the reason if the candidate says the LED is lit.*\n\n**(d)** [2 marks]\n\n- **Each dry cell supplies 1.5 V** (1 mark).\n- **Two cells joined in series add up: 1.5 + 1.5 = 3 V** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: The word 'series' or a correct description of it is needed for the second mark.*\n\n### Question 2 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- A - **furnace or boiler** (1 mark).\n- B - **turbine** (1 mark).\n- C - **generator** (1 mark).\n- D - **transmission pylon (power lines)** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'Chimney' written for A earns no mark; the chimney only carries away the waste gases.*\n\n**(b)** [3 marks]\n\n- **A: chemical energy of the fuel to heat energy** (1 mark).\n- **B: heat energy of the steam to kinetic energy of the turbine** (1 mark).\n- **C: kinetic energy to electrical energy** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: The three changes must be in the right order.*\n\n**(c)** [3 marks]\n\n- Any THREE of: **the heat comes from splitting uranium nuclei in a reactor, not from burning fuel**; **no smoke or carbon dioxide is given off**; **a very small mass of fuel gives a great deal of energy**; **it produces radioactive waste**; **it is far more costly to build** (1 mark each).\n  - *Marking note: A point that is true of BOTH stations, such as 'it uses a turbine', earns no mark.*\n\n### Question 3 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- Any FOUR of: **carbon dioxide adds to global warming**; **smoke and soot cause breathing diseases**; **sulphur dioxide causes acid rain**; **hot water kills fish in the river**; **oil spills pollute land and water**; **noise pollution**; **a non-renewable fuel is used up** (1 mark each).\n  - *Marking note: Two answers that both say 'air pollution' count as one.*\n\n**(b)** [3 marks]\n\n- Any THREE of: **fit filters or scrubbers to the chimneys**; **use cleaner fuel such as natural gas**; **use more solar, wind and hydro power**; **cool the water before returning it**; **site stations away from homes and plant trees**; **save electricity so that less is generated** (1 mark each).\n  - *Marking note: 'Stop making electricity' is not a practical measure and earns no mark.*\n\n**(c)** [3 marks]\n\n- **Agree that it gives off no smoke and no carbon dioxide** (1 mark).\n- **But it produces radioactive waste that stays dangerous for a very long time** (1 mark).\n- **And an accident or leak would release harmful radiation (accept: warm water still harms aquatic life)** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: A reply that merely says 'he is wrong' earns no mark."
