        "number": 1,
        "marks": 12,
        "text": "Fig. 1 shows a ball of mass 0.5 kg held at the top of a smooth slope, at a height **h** of 3.2 m above the ground. The ball is released and rolls down the slope, passing the points lettered **A**, **B** and **C**. (Take g = 10 m/s2.)\n\n\n\n*Fig. 1: A ball released at the top of a slope.*\n\n**(a)** Name the form of mechanical energy possessed by the ball at **A** and at **C**.  **[2 marks]**\n\n**(b)** Describe what happens to the energy of the ball as it rolls from **A** through **B** to **C**.  **[3 marks]**\n\n**(c)** Calculate:\n\n(i) the potential energy of the ball at **A**;  **[2 marks]**\n\n(ii) the speed of the ball at **C**, assuming all the potential energy is changed into kinetic energy.  **[2 marks]**\n\n**(d)** In a real experiment the speed measured at **C** was less than the value calculated in (c)(ii). Explain this, and state what happens to the missing energy.  **[3 marks]**\n\n---"
