        "text": "Fig. 1 shows three farms seen in one farming district. On farm **A** maize, cassava and cowpea are all growing together in the same field. On farm **B** maize is grown on one part of the land while a goat and a fowl are kept in a pen on the other part. On farm **C** the land is divided into three plots: two have been left to bush and only the third is under crops.\n\n\n\n*Fig. 1: Three farms seen in one farming district.*\n\n**(a)** Name the farming system practised on farm **A**, farm **B** and farm **C**.  **[3 marks]**\n\n**(b)** State TWO advantages the farmer on farm **B** has over the farmer on farm **A**, and TWO difficulties the farmer on farm **B** may face.  **[4 marks]**\n\n**(c)** Explain why the farmer on farm **C** has left two of his plots to bush, and state ONE reason why this system is becoming difficult to practise in Ghana today.  **[3 marks]**\n\n---"
