        "text": "During a health week, a nurse visited a junior high school at Bolgatanga and spoke to the pupils about food. She showed them pictures of a child who was thin, weak and often ill beside a child of the same age who was active and healthy.\n\n**(a)** (i) What is food?  **[2 marks]**\n\n(ii) Name FOUR nutrients found in food.  **[2 marks]**\n\n**(b)** State FOUR reasons why human beings need to eat.  **[4 marks]**\n\n**(c)** Describe FOUR differences the pupils would see between the starved child and the healthy child, and state what should be done to help the starved child.  **[4 marks]**\n\n---"
