    "markingScheme": "*General rules: (1) Accept any other correct and relevant answer. (2) The names of the stages must be used correctly: 'maggot' is accepted for larva, but 'caterpillar' and 'nymph' are not. (3) In a drawing or a flow chart, marks are for the correct stages, the correct order and the arrows that join them, not for beauty. (4) Where a candidate gives more answers than are asked for, mark only the first ones up to the number required. (5) Malaria is not a housefly-borne disease and earns no mark anywhere in this paper. (6) Do not deduct marks for spelling unless the meaning is changed.)*\n\n### Question 1 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- A - **larva** (accept: maggot) (1 mark).\n- B - **adult (adult housefly)** (1 mark).\n- C - **egg (eggs)** (1 mark).\n- D - **pupa** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'Caterpillar' or 'nymph' written for A earns no mark.*\n\n**(b)** [2 marks]\n\n- **C, A, D, B** (2 marks; 1 mark if only one letter is out of place).\n  - *Marking note: Accept the same order written in a circle, for example A, D, B, C, provided the sequence is unbroken.*\n\n**(c)** [2 marks]\n\n- A - **the larva feeds on the rotting matter and grows quickly** (1 mark).\n- D - **the insect rests inside a hard case, does not feed, and changes into the adult** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'It sleeps' alone is not accepted for D; the change into the adult must be shown.*\n\n**(d)** [2 marks]\n\n- **The adult lays eggs, which start the same stages again** (1 mark).\n- **The same stages follow one another in the same order over and over again** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: A candidate who writes only 'because it is round' earns no mark.*\n\n### Question 2 (12 marks)\n\n**(a)** [3 marks]\n\n- J - **food left uncovered (open) on a table, with flies on it** (1 mark).\n- K - **a heap of refuse (rubbish) with flies around it** (1 mark).\n- L - **food covered with a net cover, with no flies on it** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: The idea of 'uncovered' at J and 'covered' at L must be clear.*\n\n**(b)** [3 marks]\n\n- **K provides food and a breeding place for the flies** (1 mark).\n- **J is open and easy to reach, and the smell attracts the flies** (1 mark).\n- **The net at L keeps the flies off the food although they can still smell it** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: Accept 'the flies cannot pass through the holes of the net' for the third mark.*\n\n**(c)** [3 marks]\n\n- Any THREE of: **they transfer disease germs to the food and cause diseases such as dysentery, diarrhoea, cholera or typhoid fever**; **they contaminate the food and cause food poisoning**; **they are a nuisance in the home and environment**; **they spoil the food so that it must be thrown away** (1 mark each).\n  - *Marking note: Malaria earns no mark; it is spread by the mosquito.*\n\n**(d)** [3 marks]\n\n- Any THREE of: **keep all food covered until it is eaten**; **clear the refuse heap and use a bin with a tight lid**; **dispose of refuse at the proper dumping site regularly**; **sweep the compound and keep gutters clean and dry**; **clear away food remains and wash plates at once** (1 mark each).\n  - *Marking note: 'Kill all the flies' is not accepted as a lasting change.*\n\n### Question 3 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- Egg - **in rotting rubbish, manure, faeces or decaying food** (1 mark).\n- Larva - **in the same rotting matter, where it feeds** (1 mark).\n- Pupa - **in the drier part of the rubbish or in the soil beneath it** (1 mark).\n- Adult - **flying about the compound, on refuse, faeces and uncovered food** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'In dirty places' may be credited once only.*\n\n**(b)** [3 marks]\n\n- **The warm, damp conditions suit the eggs and larvae** (1 mark).\n- **Rotting rubbish and waste, which are food and breeding places, are plentiful** (1 mark).\n- **The life cycle is completed in only one to three weeks and many eggs are laid each time** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: Accept 'the flies breed faster because it is warm and wet' for 1 mark only.*\n\n**(c)** [3 marks]\n\n- Any THREE of: **the eggs and larvae can"
