    "markingScheme": "*General rules: (1) Accept any other correct and relevant answer. (2) In a drawing, marks are for the correct shape and the correct labels, not for beauty; every label line must touch the part it names. (3) Accept the singular or the plural form of the name of an organelle, for example mitochondrion or mitochondria. (4) Where a candidate gives more answers than are asked for, mark only the first ones up to the number required. (5) 'Cell wall' and 'cell membrane' are different parts; one written for the other earns no mark. (6) Do not deduct marks for spelling unless the meaning is changed.)*\n\n### Question 1 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [5 marks]\n\n- A - **cell membrane** (1 mark).\n- B - **cytoplasm** (1 mark).\n- C - **nucleus** (1 mark).\n- D - **mitochondrion** (1 mark).\n- E - **vacuole** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'Cell wall' written for A earns no mark; an animal cell has no cell wall.*\n\n**(b)** [3 marks]\n\n- A - **controls what enters and leaves the cell** (accept: holds the cell together) (1 mark).\n- C - **controls the activities of the cell** (1 mark).\n- D - **releases energy from food (respiration)** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'It protects the cell' alone is not accepted for C.*\n\n**(c)** [2 marks]\n\n- Any TWO of: **there is no cell wall and the shape is irregular**; **there are no chloroplasts**; **there is no large central vacuole**; **the nucleus is not pushed to one side** (1 mark each).\n  - *Marking note: The reason must be visible in the figure.*\n\n### Question 2 (12 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- (i) **The smallest unit of a living organism** (1 mark) **that can carry out the activities of life / from which all living things are built** (1 mark).\n- (ii) Any TWO of: **both plants and animals are made of cells**; **the cell is the basic unit of all living things**; **cells are too small to be seen without a microscope** (1 mark each).\n  - *Marking note: 'A small thing in the body' earns no mark in (i).*\n\n**(b)** [4 marks]\n\n- Cytoplasm - **where the organelles lie and most reactions of the cell take place** (1 mark).\n- Nucleus - **controls the activities of the cell** (1 mark).\n- Mitochondrion - **releases energy from food** (1 mark).\n- Ribosome - **makes proteins** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: The table must be copied; one correct function each is enough.*\n\n**(c)** [4 marks]\n\n- **A rounded cell with an irregular outline and no cell wall** (1 mark).\n- **Four correct parts shown and named** - cell membrane, cytoplasm, nucleus, mitochondrion (accept vacuole or ribosome) (2 marks; 1 mark if only two or three are correct).\n- **Each label written outside the drawing with a straight line touching the part named** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: A drawing that includes a cell wall or chloroplasts loses the first mark.*\n\n### Question 3 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [5 marks]\n\n- P - **cell wall** (1 mark).\n- Q - **cell membrane** (1 mark).\n- R - **nucleus** (1 mark).\n- S - **chloroplast** (1 mark).\n- T - **vacuole (large central vacuole)** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: P and Q must not be interchanged; the cell wall is the outer line.*\n\n**(b)** [3 marks]\n\n- P - **gives the cell a fixed shape and gives support and protection** (1 mark).\n- S - **makes food for the plant by photosynthesis / holds the chlorophyll** (1 mark).\n- T - **stores cell sap and keeps the cell firm** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'It protects the cell' alone is not enough for P; the idea of shape or support is needed.*\n\n**(c)** [2 marks]\n\n- (i) **The root is in the soil where there is no light, so no food can be made there** (1 mark).\n- (ii) **Food made in the leaves is carried down to the root through the stem** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'Because it is not green' is accepted for (i) only if the absence of light is also stated.*\n\n### Question 4 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- Cell wall - **present / absent** (1 mark).\n- Chloroplast - **present / absent** (1 mark).\n- Vacuole - **present in both, large and central in the plant cell but small in the animal cell** (1 mark).\n- Nucleu"
