    "markingScheme": "*General rules: (1) Accept any other correct and relevant answer. (2) Accept the local name of a material provided the material meant is clear. (3) A chemical symbol must be written with a capital first letter and, where there is a second letter, a small letter; 'NA' for sodium earns no mark. (4) Where a candidate gives more answers than are asked for, mark only the first ones up to the number required. (5) Diagrams and tables need not be works of art; marks are for correct entries and correct labels. (6) Do not deduct marks for spelling unless the meaning is changed.)*\n\n### Question 1 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [3 marks]\n\n- P - **solid** (1 mark).\n- Q - **liquid** (1 mark).\n- R - **gas** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: One mark for each correct state; no half marks.*\n\n**(b)** [3 marks]\n\n- P - **the particles are closely packed in a regular pattern and the material keeps its own shape** (1 mark).\n- Q - **the particles are close together but irregular and there is a flat surface; the material takes the shape of the bottom of the jar** (1 mark).\n- R - **the particles are far apart, moving, and spread through the whole jar** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: The reason must come from the figure; 'because it is a solid' earns no mark.*\n\n**(c)** [2 marks]\n\n- (i) **It escapes and spreads out into the room** (1 mark).\n- (ii) **The particles of a gas move freely in all directions, so a gas spreads to fill the space available** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'It finishes' alone earns no mark in (i).*\n\n**(d)** [2 marks]\n\n- P - any solid, e.g. **salt, sugar, charcoal, stone, cooking pot** (1 mark).\n- Q - any liquid, e.g. **water, palm oil, kerosene, milk** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: The example must be found in a home; 'iron ore' is not accepted.*\n\n### Question 2 (12 marks)\n\n**(a)** [6 marks]\n\n- Solids - **chalk**, **river sand** (1 mark each).\n- Liquids - **borehole water**, **groundnut oil** (1 mark each).\n- Gases - **cooking gas**, **air in the balloon** (1 mark each).\n  - *Marking note: A material entered under the wrong heading earns no mark; the table must be copied.*\n\n**(b)** [3 marks]\n\n- (i) **Fixed shape and fixed volume** (1 mark).\n- (ii) **No fixed shape, but fixed volume** (1 mark).\n- (iii) **Neither fixed shape nor fixed volume** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: Both halves of the answer are needed for the mark in each case.*\n\n**(c)** [3 marks]\n\n- **Push an inverted empty glass (or blow up a balloon) into a bucket of water** (1 mark).\n- **Observation: the water does not fill the glass and the inside remains dry (the balloon swells)** (1 mark).\n- **Conclusion: the air (gas) in the glass occupies the space** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: An activity with no stated observation earns 1 mark only.*\n\n### Question 3 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- Any FOUR of: **drinking**; **cooking**; **bathing or washing the body**; **washing clothes and utensils**; **cleaning the house and compound**; **watering plants**; **giving to livestock** (1 mark each).\n  - *Marking note: Two answers that mean the same thing, such as 'washing' and 'washing clothes', score once.*\n\n**(b)** [2 marks]\n\n- Any TWO of: **helps in digestion**; **carries digested food and oxygen round the body in the blood**; **removes waste as urine and sweat**; **controls body temperature** (1 mark each).\n  - *Marking note: Uses outside the body earn no mark here.*\n\n**(c)** [2 marks]\n\n- Any TWO of: **water is scarce, especially in the dry season**; **it costs time, labour and money to fetch**; **it cannot be replaced at once when wasted**; **uncovered or wasted water breeds mosquitoes and causes disease**; **all life in the village depends on it** (1 mark each).\n  - *Marking note: Two distinct reasons are required.*\n\n**(d)** [2 marks]\n\n- Liquid: **palm oil, groundnut oil, kerosene, petrol or diesel** (1 mark).\n- Use: **cooking** / **lighting a lamp or stove** / **fuel for vehicles and machines** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: The use must match the liquid named.*\n\n### Question 4 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)**"
