    "markingScheme": "*General rules: (1) Accept any other correct and relevant answer. (2) The name of a career must be the name of the worker or of the field, for example 'pharmacist' or 'pharmacy'; 'he works in a hospital' is not the name of a career. (3) Where a scientist is named, the field of work and the contribution must agree; a correct name with the wrong work earns no mark. (4) Titles such as Professor and Doctor need not be written, and spelling of the names is marked generously provided the person is clearly recognisable. (5) Where a candidate gives more answers than are asked for, mark only the first ones up to the number required. (6) Do not deduct marks for spelling unless the meaning is changed.)*\n\n### Question 1 (12 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- A - **laboratory scientist or technician (accept biologist, chemist)** (1 mark).\n- B - **doctor or nurse (accept any named health worker)** (1 mark).\n- C - **agricultural scientist (accept agronomist, soil scientist)** (1 mark).\n- D - **civil engineer (accept architect, surveyor)** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'He works in a laboratory' is not the name of a career.*\n\n**(b)** [4 marks]\n\n- A - **tests samples so that disease is detected and food and water are safe** (1 mark).\n- B - **treats the sick and immunises people, saving lives** (1 mark).\n- C - **improves crops and methods, so more food is produced** (1 mark).\n- D - **designs safe roads, bridges, dams and buildings** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'He earns money' is not a benefit to the people.*\n\n**(c)** [2 marks]\n\n- **Integrated science and mathematics (accept English for one)** (1 mark).\n- **Reason: science supplies the knowledge and mathematics the measurement and calculation that all these careers require** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: Subjects named with no reason earn 1 mark only.*\n\n**(d)** [2 marks]\n\n- **A scientist carries out research and makes discoveries in a field of science** (1 mark).\n- **A science educator studies and improves the teaching and learning of science (trains teachers, writes books, develops the curriculum)** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'One is cleverer than the other' earns no mark.*\n\n### Question 2 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [3 marks]\n\n- (i) **Alexander Fleming** (1 mark).\n- (ii) **Penicillin** (1 mark).\n- (iii) **A substance from the mould had killed or stopped the growth of the bacteria** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'Antibiotic' alone is accepted for (ii) only if penicillin is named.*\n\n**(b)** [3 marks]\n\n- Q - **the substance is tested and studied in the laboratory and the results recorded** (1 mark).\n- R - **the medicine is manufactured in a factory and packed** (1 mark).\n- S - **the patient is treated and recovers** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: Credit any clear wording of each stage.*\n\n**(c)** [2 marks]\n\n- **Science makes the discovery and tests it** (1 mark).\n- **Industry manufactures it in large quantities so that it reaches the people** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: A general statement with no reference to the stages earns 1 mark at most.*\n\n**(d)** [2 marks]\n\n- Any TWO of: **keen observation**; **curiosity and an open mind**; **patience and careful follow-up work**; **careful recording and reporting of findings** (1 mark each).\n  - *Marking note: 'He was clever' is too vague for a mark.*\n\n### Question 3 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- Allotey - **mathematics and physics** (1 mark).\n- Oduro - **food science (food and crop processing)** (1 mark).\n- Addy - **biochemistry and the biological sciences** (1 mark).\n- Anamuah-Mensah - **science education** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: A field written against the wrong person earns no mark.*\n\n**(b)** [3 marks]\n\n- **Prof. Theophilus Ossei-Anto** (1 mark); **Prof. Christian Anthony-Krueger** (1 mark).\n- **They improve the teaching and learning of science, so that more pupils understand it and take up science careers** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: Any other correctly named Ghanaian science educator is accepted.*\n\n**(c)** [3 marks]\n\n- Any THREE of: **it shows that Ghana"
