        "text": "Mercury and Venus are the two planets whose paths lie between the Earth and the Sun. Mercury goes round the Sun once in about 88 Earth days and Venus in about 225 Earth days. The Earth takes about 365 days.\n\n**(a)** Copy and complete the table below in your answer booklet.  **[4 marks]**\n\n| | Mercury | Venus |\n|---|---|---|\n| Position from the Sun | ......... | ......... |\n| One property peculiar to the planet | ......... | ......... |\n\n**(b)** Venus is farther from the Sun than Mercury, yet Venus is the hotter of the two. Explain this.  **[3 marks]**\n\n**(c)** (i) How many times does Mercury go round the Sun while the Earth goes round once? Show your working and give your answer to the nearest whole number.  **[2 marks]**\n\n(ii) What does your answer tell you about the length of a year on Mercury?  **[1 mark]**\n\n**(d)** Venus is often called the morning star or the evening star. Explain why this name is given to it and state why the name is not strictly correct.  **[2 marks]**\n\n---"
