    "markingScheme": "*General rules: (1) Accept any other correct and relevant answer. (2) The terms biodegradable, non-biodegradable, segregation, composting, recycling and reuse must be used correctly; 'reuse' written for 'recycle' earns no mark. (3) Where a practice is asked for, the answer must state an action; 'keep the place clean' alone is too vague. (4) In classification tasks, mark each entry separately and do not carry an error forward. (5) Where a candidate gives more answers than are asked for, mark only the first ones up to the number required. (6) Do not deduct marks for spelling unless the meaning is changed.)*\n\n### Question 1 (12 marks)\n\n**(a)** [4 marks]\n\n- A - **organic (food or kitchen) waste** (1 mark).\n- B - **plastic waste** (1 mark).\n- C - **glass and metal waste** (1 mark).\n- D - **paper waste** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: Accept 'biodegradable waste' for A and D only if the material is also named.*\n\n**(b)** [4 marks]\n\n- A - **biodegradable** (1 mark).\n- B - **non-biodegradable** (1 mark).\n- C - **non-biodegradable** (1 mark).\n- D - **biodegradable** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: Mark each entry separately.*\n\n**(c)** [2 marks]\n\n- **Biodegradable waste is broken down by micro-organisms into simple substances** (1 mark).\n- **Non-biodegradable waste is not broken down and stays in the environment for a very long time** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'One rots and the other does not' is accepted for the first mark only if decay is clearly meant.*\n\n**(d)** [2 marks]\n\n- **Sort it into a separate container and send it for recycling (accept: bury it safely in a pit)** (1 mark).\n- **Because glass and metal do not decay; broken glass causes injury and tins collect water in which mosquitoes breed** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: 'Burn it' earns no mark.*\n\n### Question 2 (8 marks)\n\n**(a)** [3 marks]\n\n- Any THREE of: **flies spread typhoid, cholera or diarrhoea**; **mosquitoes breeding in the tins spread malaria**; **rats and cockroaches spread disease**; **the smell and smoke affect breathing**; **sharp objects cause injury** (1 mark each).\n  - *Marking note: A disease named without its link to the heap still earns the mark if the link is obvious.*\n\n**(b)** [3 marks]\n\n- **The organic waste is decaying, being broken down by bacteria and fungi** (1 mark).\n- **Gases such as ammonia and hydrogen sulphide are released, and these smell bad** (1 mark).\n- **Mosquitoes lay eggs in the still water and breed there, spreading malaria** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: Accept 'rotting' for decay.*\n\n**(c)** [2 marks]\n\n- Any TWO of: **burning plastics and rubber releases poisonous smoke and gases that pollute the air and harm the lungs**; **the fire may spread and destroy property**; **useful material that could be composted or recycled is destroyed** (1 mark each).\n  - *Marking note: 'It is against the law' earns no mark without a scientific reason.*\n\n### Question 3 (10 marks)\n\n**(a)** [3 marks]\n\n- **Reduce: produce less waste by using less and avoiding unnecessary items** (1 mark).\n- **Reuse: use an article again as it is, instead of throwing it away** (1 mark).\n- **Recycle: process used material into new articles** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: An example alone, with no explanation, earns no mark.*\n\n**(b)** [3 marks]\n\n- **Reduce: one sound example, such as a refillable bottle instead of daily sachets** (1 mark).\n- **Reuse: one sound example, such as tins used for seedlings** (1 mark).\n- **Recycle: one sound example, such as collecting plastic bottles for a recycling centre** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: An example placed under the wrong term earns no mark.*\n\n**(c)** [2 marks]\n\n- **Separating waste into different containers according to its kind** (1 mark).\n- **So that each kind can be composted, reused or recycled instead of being dumped** (1 mark).\n  - *Marking note: Accept 'sorting' for segregation.*\n\n**(d)** [2 marks]\n\n- **Three sensible labels, such as organic waste, plastics and paper** (1 mark).\n- **A correct item named for each bin** (1 mark).\n  - *"
